1.1.text:
Article 17

1. The provision of protection services for women as referred to in Article 16 letter e shall be in the form of victim identification, legal assistance, medical rehabilitation, psychosocial rehabilitation, social reintegration, repatriation assistance, or other forms.
2. The provision of protection services for women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be given to women:
a. victims of violence;
b. victims of human trafficking;
c. in conflict-prone and disaster areas;
d. workers;
e. elderly;
f. persons with disabilities;
g. victims of sexual exploitation;
h. heads of households; and
i. other vulnerable groups.

Article 16

The Regent in implementing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women shall undertake efforts to: a. coordinate the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women among Regional Work Units;
b. cooperate with Regencies/Cities within one Province, and cooperation between Regencies/Cities in other Provinces in the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women in accordance with the provisions of statutory regulations;
c. strengthen the institutional capacity of gender mainstreaming for the implementation of policies, programs and activities for the protection of women;
d. facilitate services for the protection of women;
e. provide services for the protection of women;
f. implement affirmative action for the protection of women; and
g. prepare a data system for the protection of women.

Article 4

1. Every woman has the right: a. to live, maintain life and improve her standard of living;
b. to live peacefully, safely, in peace, happily, prosperously physically and spiritually;
c. to a good and healthy living environment;
d. to live in a family within the bonds of lawful marriage;
e. to choose the work she likes and is also entitled to fair employment conditions;
f. to receive fair wages in accordance with her work that is comparable and commensurate with human dignity.
2. A lawful marriage can only take place based on the free will of the woman and the man in accordance with statutory regulations.

(3) Every woman who is in a condition of disability, old age, pregnancy, has the right to obtain special facilities and treatment.

(4) Every elderly woman, with physical disability and/or mental disability, has the right to obtain care, education, training, and special assistance at the expense of the regional government, to ensure a decent life in accordance with human dignity.

The rights of women as referred to in paragraph (3) and paragraph (4) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

